1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Hello everyone, my name is Abdurrahman Assegaf.

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:11,500
In this video, I am presenting our solution for the ARC Prize 2026 Paper Track competition.

3
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:18,000
ARC-AGI is the benchmark for Artificial General Intelligence created by François Chollet and Mike Knoop.

4
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:24,500
It evaluates fluid intelligence—the ability to learn novel reasoning rules from minimal input-output demonstrations.

5
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:31,000
To tackle this challenge, we developed the Dual-System Neuro-Symbolic Synthesis architecture.

6
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:37,500
This system is composed of two primary modules: System 1 and System 2.

7
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:44,000
System 1 is an ultra-fast Domain-Specific Language search engine running in under 200 milliseconds per task.

8
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:51,000
It deterministically tests core priors such as symmetry, gravity, object segmentation, and topological hole filling without hallucination.

9
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:58,000
System 2 utilizes an LLM Program Synthesizer with an execution sandbox verifier and Reflexion self-correction loop.

10
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:05,000
Now, let's explore the live interactive dashboard built with Streamlit.

11
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:11,500
Here on Task 00d62c1b, the solver successfully discovered the fill_enclosed transformation in just 0.01 seconds.

12
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:18,000
Similarly, for gravity task 1e0a9b12 and object cropping task 1f85a75f, the solver produces 100% exact match predictions.

13
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:25,000
Across all 400 official ARC training tasks, System 1 solved 25 tasks instantaneously.

14
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:31,500
This dual approach saves over 90% of compute and eliminates spatial hallucinations.

15
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:38,000
All source code, datasets, and paper drafts are fully open-sourced on our GitHub repository.

16
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:44,000
